   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the urban development corporation act, in relation to the restore New York's communities initiative",
    "basePrintNo": "S7285",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7285-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §16-n, UDC Act",
    "lawSection": "New York State Urban Development Corporation Act",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7285\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the urban development corporation act, in relation to\nthe restore New York's communities initiative\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL :\n\nThe bill would enhance the Economic State Development Corporation's\n(ESD) ability to utilize the Restore New York's Communities Initiative\n(\"Restore NY\") by allowing reconstructed buildings in eligible\nlocations to be used in a manner beyond the use of a previously\nexisting building at the same location.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend paragraph (b) of subdivision 1 of\nsection 16-n of the Urban Development Corporation Act to remove the\nRestore NY requirement that reconstructed buildings in eligible\nlocations be used in a manner similar to previously existing buildings\nat the same location.\n\nSection 2 would make the bill effective immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis bill would provide ESD with greater flexibility in administering\nRestore NY by allowing creative new uses of reconstructed buildings at\neligible locations. Currently, Restore NY requires that reconstructed\nbuildings be used in a manner similar to a previously existing\nbuilding at the same location.\n\nThe bill would remove the similar use requirement, enhancing ESD's\nability to assist with the revitalization of properties. While\nwell-intentioned, in many cases it is difficult or not desirable to\nmeet this requirement. Additional flexibility would allow for the\nreplacement of antiquated uses with those that reflect the area's\ncurrent economic needs and assets.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
